|||||||||Our story begins on a midnight walk... or in Gish and his tarball kids' case, a midnight roll. A roll rudely interrupted by a rancid little creature of the sewers...|Help!|Pfew! I know that stench... Hera's henchman from the Sewers of Dross!|Aw, don't you go worryin' about your little tarballs, Gish. We'll take gooood care a'them! Ahahaha! *cough*|Daddy! Help!|Shut yo' tarhole you little creep! Oh, Hera says hi. Hahaha! *cough* Smell ya later!|Hera? As in ex-girlfriend Hera? As in Hera who I threw into the lava Hera? And what does she want with my Eyelings anyways? This can only mean one thing... a sequel. Time to kick some ass and get to the bottom of this!|Gish becomes 'slick' when you change his surface by clicking the bottom left corner of the screen (his surface becomes brownish). When Gish is slick he can easily slide through narrow passages, but can't climb walls.|smazano|Buttons open doors and activate lifts. The light near the button is green if the lift/door is activated.|This wall is too slippery for Gish to climb.|Gish jumps best when he's flattened. Point up in the direction from Gish to jump. Keep the pointer there to jump higher. Stick to the top of the wall.|Gish becomes 'sticky' when you change his surface by clicking the bottom left corner of the screen (his surface becomes grayish). When sticky, Gish can climb the walls and ceiling.|You found a secret passage! Find more to unlock bonus maps. There is at least one on every level so keep your eyes open!|Whoa! That was one heck of a ride, baby!||Hm, that's strange, the water should be frozen at this temperature...|Dad! I chewed my way out of the sack and escaped!|Good boy! Don't forget to floss when you get home.|Aw, Dad!|Spikes and enemies can hurt you! You can see your health level in the top left corner of the screen. Raise it by collecting tarballs just like the ones next to you now.|Well lookee what we've got here. If it ain't our good ol' buddy Gish. I guess you was thinkin' you could just walk in here and see Hera? Hahaha! Hear that boys? Whaddya say we show our pal here how we look after guests?|Oh, is there complimentary ice cream?|Mr. Questionmark says, don't even try to kill the boss; explore the room instead.|And now for something completely different - Egypt! Don't ask me how we got here!|How did we get here?|I said...|Whatever.|This button must be kept down, otherwise the lift will stop. There is a box nearby, push it onto this button. You know the switch is activated when the light is green.|puf, huf... finally, at the top of the hill. What a gorgeous view from here! Walls, dust and dead rats!|Gah, more water! And I was just starting to dry off!||Stick to the ground and move carefully around the corner or you'll get hurt!|Aah, warmth at last! Wait, what the... Hell?|I think I just found an ancient septic tank.... pfew!|Gasp. *catches breath* Dad! That dirty old pile of phooey came back!|Hmm. Looks like we need a more permanent solution.|When you meet an enemy, you can sometimes just run away from him.|You can also squish enemies by jumping on them when Gish is angry (click on his body).|Well boys, it's a-lookin like our little tar buddy's come back for more. I ain't sittin' on no trapdoor this time! Now squish him, boys!|What's a matter? Too scared to fight me by your lonesome?|Bad news - I just got even more angry!|Hmm, something tells me this heavy box could help me get out of here. I just better not get in the way...|Here's a little hint in case you get stuck - even your blood can push a button... make of that what you will.|Well lookee who's got himself all trapped up! Poor little Gishy. Hope you're not claustrophobic! *evil laughter*|Legend has it that 6 noble pharaohs placed 6 hidden treasures in 6 hallowed rooms and that 1 tarball would plunder them all.|Say, d'you see any other tarballs round here? Me neither! Woot!|Looks like I'm in for a slide... I knew I should've packed my snowboard!|You've gotta love the sound of squishing flesh, right? Right?!|You need to get this box to a button on the right side of this room. Stick to it and then throw it (by clicking the Gish's body). You can also throw it at an enemy to kill it (target its head). If the box gets destroyed, it will respawn at its original position.|Throwing the box up might seem hard, but after some practice it's a piece of cake.|Pew! Smells like a sewer in here... well, whaddya know, it IS a sewer!|Dad! I'm t-trapped! Over h-here!|Hold on! I'll have you out in no time!|Thanks Dad! Now I can help you too - just bounce on me to jump higher!|Only one amber piece? You've got to be kidding me!|Not at all.|*censored*|Don't worry, you're safe for now.|I saw Hera! Look at my tar, I'm shaking! She's sure terrifying, Dad!|Little eye says it's time to rock and roll!|Remember this: try to stick with her.|How'd you know that?|Oh, you know, some kid on Gamefaqs.|I forgot my tar-tight diving suit... and I feel so sexy in it too!|So Hera really IS alive...|Ah, my darling Gish... don't look so surprised - do you really think lava would kill me? Ha! Lava can't harm you when you're as hot as I am! And now I'm going to be the most beautiful ball of tar ever!|Not catch you? Last I knew, you were slower than a legless drunk.|How dare you! We'll see who's legless here!|Um... actually we both are...|Shut Up! *starts to run*|Ha! Too slow you are, my Love. And now for the main course!|Bling bling!|Arg, Egypt. Probably loads of puzzles and traps just like last time. I hope you know what you're doing, thing which gets in my head and tells me what to do...|Um, I think Gish may be referring to *YOU* there.|Smoking and drinking is bad for your health... and so am I.|but...|Mr. Questionmark would like to point out that you can break some springs if you create enough tension.|You know, it's weird. I always pictured Hell as being a bit more, I dunno, scary...|Fresh meat!|Ok, I'll be honest, I'm still not really scared... maybe you could work on that?|*cough cough* Dad! This place, it's h-haunted! Run!|I ain't afraid of no ghost. |You haven't seen this one yet... *shudders*|A visitor! It's been... well, a while. Now I'm terribly sorry, but I suspect now that I must take your soul. It's a curse, you see. It's all in small print at the entrance to my tomb.|Uh huh. So, I see. And how were you thinking of doing that?|I shall cut you into small pieces with my super sharp sword, then catch your diminishing soul in the plastic bag I have with me.|How did my son put it? Ah yes... Ruuuuun!!!|Please! Anything but the light! Anything!|Anything, you say? *evil flash in his eyes*|Whatever you've got in mind, don't.|Oh my. So many choices... Maybe I should leave a trail of stones like that book... or was it crumbs? I don't have either anyways.|The only way you're gonna get through this door is over my big dead ass.|So be it.|God this place stinks. Or is it my socks? Wait, can't be them... no feet.|So... we meet again. Do ignore my last performance; we all have our 'off days', don't you think? Now, there still is the pressing issue of me needing your soul. Unfortunately my tomb was built a few thousand years before central heating and it actually needs souls to be anything approaching comfortably warm.|Let me get this straight - you expect me to be your central heating?|No, Mr. Gish, I expect for you to die.|Warmth! That's much better, thank you! Terribly sorry about the upset. All's well that ends well, I suppose. See you in the afterlife I'll wager!|Your alignment has been changed to 'CHAOTIC GOOD'|What the heck is chaotic good?|Oops, sorry, wrong game...|Jeez, so many buttons!|Right, it's like mission control in here...|Mission what? Anyway, I should take a closer look at what these buttons do.|Whoa... this bridge seems to be held together by will power alone!|*huff puff* That's right! Now hurry up, I can't focus my will much longer!|One false step and I'm cooked.|This looks like fuuuuun!|Uggh, I feel like I just ate English food and then went on a rollercoaster while standing upside down.|Mm, I like English food. Shepherd's pie, yum yum!|You, sir, are strange.|You didn't think you could get rid of me so easily, Cutie, did you?|Actually, I did.|Well then you've got a lot to learn little boy. Look how little you are compared to me! And in 3 minutes I'll be even larger, after eating your kids!|Don't be so sure. What could you do to stop me?|Perhaps a double-reinforced door will do the trick? *evil laughter*|Mr. Questionmark points out that you can throw Hera by clicking on Gish's body if you are stuck to her. |Now, where's my knife and fork?|Money money money; swinging is so funny, tra la la la la!|Oops! Someone's been careless...|*blushes slightly* Sorry, I'll take more care in the future. *giggle*|Solid ground at last! If I had feet, they'd be pretty well roasted by now.|Hmm, strange smells, rats... let me guess, another sewer!|*sniff sniff* Ugh, what's that smell? Did you have beans for lunch or what?|What the hell is that? It's got more teeth than a pool of sharks!|And it's got tentacles coming out of the ground, too!|Aha! A weak spot!|Who's your daddy?! You don't like this at all, do you!|I wonder who stuck all those skulls on pikes? And where did he get so many skulls?|I don't think you want to know.|Hey! Did you put these skulls on spikes?!|Uhm... I... only this one! Looks funny!|Let's see how funny *your* skull is then!|Mr. Questionmark points out that you can break some springs. This one, for example.|This seems like a storage area to me. You know, oil, grain, gold and...|Bling bling?|Lucky me! Here's dinner!|...and is heavily guarded.|Just taking out the tentacles isn't going to work this time. Hmm, seems hungry... Wonder if he's ever tasted tarball?|Well, I hope I give you indigestion.|Hah! Looks like you bit off a bit more than you could chew!|Strike now, while the creature is doubled over in pain!|Look! A boat!|No, it's just a block.|When I close my eyes, I see myself as a captain, with a bit hat and a black flag, bravely cruising dangerous waters...|...Lava, you mean lava! Well, now that you mention it, it does look rather sturdy...|...So, if I put this box on the second button... no, so if I... no... *clouds of steam start to come up from him*|Hey, take it easy! You're here to do as you're told. Not to think!|*grabs a skull from the ground* To be sticky, or not to be sticky? That is the question.|Jeez, it's like this place is melting into lava! There must be something really hot in here.|Or *someone*. Someone grey and blobby.|Hmm. Hera's skin sticks to me like chewing gum to the bottom of my shoe.|And now, you and I will stay here. Together. Forever! Forget about Brea! Think of the life we would share here!|Stay together? Here with you? After all that stuff about eating my kids?!|They are children of a human! Wake up, Gish! You can't be with a member of such a subrace! You are destined to be with me!|Well, in that case, it's time to kick destiny's ass!|Nooo! Then we must die together!|The walls of the cave are closing in to crush you!|*dramatic voice* and this is how our little drama ends...|Hang on, there's one more thing to do!|Ready! Aim! Fire!|Wait, wha- *kaboom*|Dad! You made it!|Sure I did! It's OK kids, you're safe now.|Er, yeah, about that...|?|It just didn't feel like a proper ending...|Alright, kids, what have you done?|Well, we kinda rigged the whole place to, well, explode.|You did WHAT?!|It's no good ending unless everything explodes, right Dad? We thought you'd be pleased.|We'll talk about this later, in the meantime.... Ruuuuun!!!|Welcome to my little playground. Feel free to play with the toys to the death. I'll be over here if you need me.|A long time ago in a sewer far away lived Gish and Hera. They were friends, close friends... lovers, actually. Like a Bonnie and Clyde of the tarball world, this infamous duo was well known for raiding tombs and sewers for trinkets and treasure.|Yeah!|Rock and roll!|If your teammate dies, you can revive him by collecting all his tarballs.|To complete a level, both of you must get to the level exit. Alive.|If you find it difficult, finish more singleplayer levels first.|Ugh, what a stench!|Smells like...|...go on, say it, like the stuff which collects when a toilet leaks. Go on, everyone says it. You might as well too.|Actually, I think he's kind of cute!|*blushes* |Ok, that's it, we're going topside, Hera. And you'd better wash your hands or you're not getting any dinner.|Bye, sweet honey... bucket!|␀␀Ìc